<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#fatwa">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A fatwa is a formal legal opinion issued by a qualified Islamic jurist. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> obtained fatwas from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki</a> jurists condemning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> as insufficiently observant, which served as religious justification for deposing them in the 1090s.</p></div>
